{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` is 789 lines and currently owns startup-handshake behavior beside health routing, certified-tool instrumentation, graceful HTTP serving, SIGTERM draining, and startup store/op-cert checks. The approved remedy is headroom through a handshake-only extraction, not a lifecycle or transport redesign. In this checkout, `mcp_server.py` continues to import `wire_health`, `run_startup_store_sweep`, and `run_mcp` from `_mcp_health`; HTTP serving is still `run_http_with_grace` in that facade.\n\n## End State\n\nA leaf `_mcp_startup_handshake.py` owns only the cohesive initialize-probe call graph: probe-host selection, ASGI request drive, bounded result record, lifespan wrapping, and handshake status. `_mcp_health` imports and re-exports the existing handshake names, remains the health/serving/orchestration facade, and retains the call from `run_http_with_grace`. `mcp_server.py` retains its present facade-level imports. The extracted leaf never imports `_mcp_health`, preventing an import cycle.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Identify the handshake-only call graph in `_mcp_health` and move it as one unit into the new leaf. Do not move the in-flight gauge, route registration, instrumentation/offload ordering, startup store/op-cert checks, HTTP transport, signal handling, or shutdown code.\n2. Re-export the moved names through `_mcp_health` and preserve lookup through that facade so current direct imports and monkeypatch targets resolve unchanged.\n3. Keep `run_http_with_grace` calling the `_mcp_health` facade installer before uvicorn serves. Avoid a leaf-to-facade import, and recensus semantic, string, dynamic-import, and monkeypatch sites before moving names.\n4. Extend focused tests around startup success/failure/timeout, public-host choice, lifespan ordering, health-record visibility, facade compatibility, and the unchanged serving/instrumentation/shutdown contracts.\n\n## File Impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` — retained health/serving facade and re-exports\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_startup_handshake.py` — new handshake-only leaf\n- `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` — only if a facade import/annotation test proves wiring needs adjustment\n- focused MCP health/startup, serving, and dynamic-patch tests\n\nCascade flag: true. Re-run the full consumer census before implementation because this is an import-boundary change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Only the startup-handshake call graph is extracted; health routing, tool instrumentation, HTTP transport, SIGTERM drain, and startup store/op-cert orchestration remain in `_mcp_health`.\n- [ ] The new leaf has no import of `_mcp_health`; `_mcp_health` remains the one-way facade and re-exports all existing handshake names.\n- [ ] `run_http_with_grace` still installs the startup handshake through `_mcp_health` before uvicorn serves, so existing facade imports and monkeypatch targets continue resolving.\n- [ ] Success, non-200, exception, and timeout handshakes retain their bounded result-record behavior; public-host selection and ASGI initialize semantics remain unchanged.\n- [ ] `wire_health` ordering, health routes, signer/op-cert status, instrumentation/offload behavior, SIGTERM handling, transport selection, and shutdown behavior remain unchanged.\n- [ ] Focused startup/health/serving tests plus module-size, complexity, lint, and typecheck gates pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788368684640215001,"uuid":"1eb24d39-a06a-4516-8424-7c73da75e975"}